From 8db1acbbe708d6abc77dd7df8a9a1d665f4d1ccf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 11:13:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Funnel Audit Trend tab, focus-blur on Show Rate Setup,
 seamless tabs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Trend tab (leak-map-trend-chart.tsx, new): a single-metric line chart of
current values across this engagement's whole audit history, using
recharts. Deliberately one metric at a time on one axis — these metrics
have different units (a % win-rate vs. a raw brief count), so a shared
multi-line chart would misstate the data; a metric picker is the
small-multiples alternative. Colors are the dataviz skill's validated
categorical slot 1, light/dark steps as CSS vars in globals.css. The API
route (leak-map-schedule/route.ts) now includes each historical run's
full topIssues instead of discarding it down to summary counts — that
was the only missing ingredient, the DB query already fetched it.

Toolbar restructure (leak-map-view.tsx): the Trend tab renders as a
seamless plain-text tab on the left (new ViewSwitcher "seamless"
variant — active/inactive is just color+weight, no background chrome),
while Overview/List is now visually "housed" as its own pill on the
right (new `containerClassName` prop). Trend only appears when a
`history` prop is supplied (leak-map-schedule.tsx's embedded call site);
the standalone single-run page has nothing to trend and doesn't show it.

Show Rate Setup (deliverables-panel.tsx): expanding one DeliverableRow
now dims + lightly blurs its (still-clickable, still-switchable)
siblings instead of leaving every closed row at full visual weight,
increasing focus on whichever one is open.

Verified with a real `pnpm run build` (not just tsc) after installing
dependencies fresh in this sandbox — compiles and type-checks clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AkznvRLnBokzbdmJ2WwaEM
